          "pull_request": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python/cpython/pulls/155936",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/155936",
            "diff_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/155936.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/155936.patch",
            "merged_at": "2026-08-23T10:10:57Z"
          },
          "body": "When `protocol_factory()` or transport creation raises for an accepted connection in `BaseSelectorEventLoop._accept_connection2()`, close the accepted socket (it would otherwise leak until garbage collection) and report the error via the loop exception handler even when debug mode is disabled.\r\n\r\nReporting stays debug-only once the transport exists, so `await waiter` failures such as SSL handshake errors from port scanners are not reported unconditionally.\r\n\r\nThis is the server-side counterpart of gh-153134 (GH-153133).\r\n\r\nThe new tests fail without the fix and pass with it. The full `test_asyncio` suite passes, including `-R 3:3` refleak runs on `test_selector_events`.\r\n\r\ncc. Pycon 2026 KR Sprint @hugovk @corona10\r\n\r\n<!-- gh-issue-number: gh-155934 -->\r\n* Issue: gh-155934\r\n<!-- /gh-issue-number -->",
          "closed_by": {
